  "language_probability": 0.9,
  "text": "Good morning Meena garu. Today Asha and I will work on asking for things with two words and on taking turns. Good morning madam. At home she is saying more words this week. Let us start with the snack game. Asha, what do you want? Well done Asha, you said want biscuit. In this game she made four two-word requests without any prompt. At home she still pulls my hand when she wants water. Next is the ball rolling game for turn taking. She waited for her turn in six out of ten rolls today, that is sixty percent. That is better than last month, she used to grab the ball every time. Meena garu, when she pulls your hand, wait and model the words want water, then give it when she tries. Okay madam, I will wait and say want water first. For home practice, play the snack game at tea time and roll a ball with her for five minutes each evening. Next week we will add colour words to her requests, like red ball and blue cup. Thank you madam, see you next week.",
